Package: mediaPlanSim
Type: Package
Title: Synthetic Multi-Insertion Exposure Data with Known Truth for Media Plans
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Manuel J.", family = "Sánchez-Franco",
           email = "majesus@us.es", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8042-3550"))
Description: Generates individual-level synthetic exposure data for media plans,
    that is, the number of contacts of each person with each vehicle, from
    explicit data-generating mechanisms: independent Beta-Binomial vehicles,
    vehicles linked by a Gaussian copula on their exposure propensities, and
    audiences made of latent segments (which can produce negative association
    between vehicles). For every mechanism it also computes the true
    distribution of the number of contacts of the plan, its reach, and the
    population moments that a media planner would feed to an exposure model:
    the reach of one and of two insertions of each vehicle and the duplication
    between vehicles. Survey data seldom contain observed exposure to several
    insertions, so these mechanisms provide a truth against which
    exposure-distribution models can be evaluated. The truth is exact for
    independent and latent-segment mechanisms and is computed by deterministic
    quasi-Monte Carlo integration for the Gaussian copula.
